    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "abae33f7-0db4-5ddb-81bf-85f151bb38fc",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=2 \\\\ 2x-5y+5z &=9 \\\\ -x+y-7z &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 5 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -7 & -15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 5 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 & -13\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "522274f1-49d7-59b0-b386-5a5f332cb03e",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
